  "notes": [
    "This contract is a fail-closed architecture boundary, not a continental identity registry, legal determination, certification, or production integration.",
    "A Member State may retain its existing foundational identity system and choose its own credential issuance and storage model; Mycelix must not infer trust from country name, document appearance, or a protocol family alone.",
    "A national profile must be based on reviewed official sources and documented authority. Empty country_profiles means no country profile is qualified by this artifact.",
    "Consent alone is not automatically a legal basis. Each relying party must establish an appropriate lawful purpose, authority, proportionality, retention, and grievance path.",
    "Country-specific eligibility rules remain with the relevant public authority and law. A successful identity proof must not be converted into a decision about benefits, immigration status, membership, credit, voting, or legal rights.",
    "Report hashes and test outputs support reproducibility but are not a digital signature or independent runner attestation."
  ]
